HEC# Ripple — Production Readiness Edge Case Test Matrix

Compiled from every bug class found across this project's debugging history. Organized by system. Each row = one test to actually run, not a theoretical concern.

---

## 1. FOCUS / WINDOW TARGETING (highest-risk area — most bugs found here)

| # | Edge case | Why it matters | Expected behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1.1 | Dictate immediately on fresh app launch (cold start), before boot-ready | Root cause of multiple bugs this project | Hotkey inert until sidecar+backend health confirmed; no partial state |
| 1.2 | Dictate, then switch to a DIFFERENT window before insert completes | Caused the WhatsApp→EGC Shopping Club misfire | Aborts with `target_window_changed`, clipboard fallback, toast — never yanks |
| 1.3 | Dictate with 2+ windows of the SAME app open (5+ Chrome windows) | Target resolution grabbed wrong window | Correct window (by hwnd, not just process name) stays targeted |
| 1.4 | Dictate, then minimize the target window mid-speech | New failure class, untested | Should detect `iconic=1` via `target_state` gate, abort before paste, not paste into nothing |
| 1.5 | Dictate on a monitor that is NOT the Windows "main display" | Root cause of the multi-week shell-steal saga | Overlay follows target's monitor (`MonitorFromWindow`), zero shell steals regardless of main-display setting |
| 1.6 | Unplug/replug external monitor WHILE app is running (not just at launch) | Never tested — display config can change mid-session | App should re-resolve monitor topology, not crash or misplace overlay |
| 1.7 | Dictate while target window is behind other windows (not minimized, just occluded) | Untested | Should still work — occlusion ≠ not-foreground |
| 1.8 | Rapid-fire: press hotkey, release, press again within <500ms | Untested — possible double-session bug | Second press should either queue cleanly or be debounced, never corrupt state |
| 1.9 | Press hotkey while a PREVIOUS dictation insert is still in-flight | Untested | Must not race — either block, queue, or cleanly cancel the first |
| 1.10 | Dictate with Windows Snap Layouts / Fancy Zones active (tiled windows) | Untested — common power-user setup | Target resolution and overlay placement should be unaffected |
| 1.11 | Dictate immediately after Windows lock/unlock (Win+L then unlock) | Untested — foreground state is unusual right after unlock | No false shell-steal, no crash |
| 1.12 | Dictate right after a Windows notification toast appears/dismisses | Untested — another transient shell surface | Should not be misidentified as a real target change |
| 1.13 | Dictate with Alt+Tab switcher UI open/closing at the same moment | Untested — another shell overlay surface | No false abort, no yank |

