## 2. INSERT LADDER / TEXT LANDING

| # | Edge case | Why it matters | Expected behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2.1 | Paste into a field that already has existing text (cursor mid-sentence) | Untested — all tests so far used empty fields | Text inserts at cursor position, doesn't overwrite/select-all by accident |
| 2.2 | Paste into a field with text SELECTED (highlighted) | Untested | Confirm intended behavior — replace selection or insert-and-deselect? Must be deliberate, not accidental |
| 2.3 | Very long dictation (500+ chars) into a slow-rendering web app | Root cause of the mid-send foreground-change bug | Chunked send with checkpoint verification holds up at this length |
| 2.4 | Very short dictation (1-2 words) | Untested | No overhead/lag disproportionate to input length |
| 2.5 | Dictate into a read-only or disabled field | Untested | Should detect non-editable and abort cleanly, not silently fail |
| 2.6 | Dictate into a field that validates/rejects input live (e.g. numeric-only field, character limit) | Untested | Graceful abort or partial-accept, clear signal to user either way |
| 2.7 | Dictate into an iframe-embedded editor (many web apps embed rich text in iframes) | Untested — accessibility tree traversal often breaks across iframe boundaries | Confirm works or fails loud, not silently |
| 2.8 | Every insert strategy fails (native_text, sendkeys, clipboard, extension all fail) | Confirmed as a designed fallback, not yet stress-tested | Text guaranteed on clipboard + visible toast, zero data loss |
| 2.9 | Clipboard already contains something important when paste-strategy fires | Untested — could silently overwrite user's existing clipboard content | Should restore original clipboard after paste, or warn user clipboard will be used |
| 2.10 | Paste into WhatsApp/Chrome when a browser extension conflicts with clipboard access | Untested | Fails loud (abort+toast), not silent |
| 2.11 | Dictate into a field, then IMMEDIATELY close that window before insert completes | Untested — target disappears entirely, not just loses focus | Must detect hwnd invalid (not just unfocused) and abort safely |
| 2.12 | RTL language insert (Urdu/Arabic) into different app types | Explicitly flagged earlier as untested | Cursor placement, selection, and text direction all correct per app |
| 2.13 | Font/script rendering check per target app (Devanagari, Arabic, CJK) | Explicitly flagged earlier as untested | No tofu-boxes; visual check per app, not just "text matched" check |

