## 4. LANGUAGE / STT

| # | Edge case | Why it matters | Expected behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| 4.1 | Clear English speech — confirm NOT misdetected as Sindhi/Urdu/Malay/Nynorsk | Confirmed recurring bug, root cause never fixed at STT level, only guarded downstream | `detected=english` reliably, or guard silently corrects every time with zero visible impact |
| 4.2 | Code-switched speech (English + Hindi in the same sentence) | Confirmed working in the meeting-notetaker diarization test — re-verify in plain dictation too | Correct mixed-script output |
| 4.3 | Romanized Hindi/Marathi (Hinglish written in Latin script) | Already documented as a known, accepted limitation | Known-limit disclosure shown to user, not silently garbled with no explanation |
| 4.4 | Background noise / multiple people talking near the mic | Untested | Reasonable degradation, not garbage output presented with false confidence |
| 4.5 | Very quiet/whispered speech | Flagged as Phase 9.6, untested | Either works or clearly indicates low-confidence, not silent failure |
| 4.6 | Language auto-detect when user has explicitly pinned a language (e.g. pinned "hi" but speaks English) | Untested | Pinned language should still produce reasonable output, not force-garble English into Hindi transliteration |

