## 5. CRASH / PROCESS STABILITY

| # | Edge case | Why it matters | Expected behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| 5.1 | First dictation into Notepad/Cursor after a FULL process kill + relaunch | The exact unresolved bug from this session | App stays alive; if it doesn't, crash log captures full stack trace |
| 5.2 | Native sidecar (ripple-native.exe) crashes independently while Electron main process stays alive | Untested — different crash domain, needs its own panic hook | Detected, logged, sidecar respawns, user sees a degraded-mode indicator rather than silent failure |
| 5.3 | Backend server becomes unreachable mid-session (not just at boot) | Untested — only boot-time health check exists | Graceful degradation/retry, clear error state, not a hang |
| 5.4 | Machine goes to sleep mid-dictation, wakes up later | Untested | No corrupted state on wake; hotkey works normally after resume |
| 5.5 | Low memory / high CPU load on the machine during dictation | Untested | Either works or fails gracefully — no crash under resource pressure |
| 5.6 | App update/restart while a dictation is in-flight | Relevant once auto-update ships | No data loss, no corrupted install |

