## 6. MEETING NOTETAKER (Phase 10)

| # | Edge case | Why it matters | Expected behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| 6.1 | Meeting stopped before 30s flush interval | Confirmed: produces empty transcript correctly | Graceful "no speech captured" note, no crash |
| 6.2 | Other audio playing (YouTube, music) during a meeting | CONFIRMED BUG — system audio loopback captures everything, not just the call | Must scope capture to the actual meeting app, or explicitly warn user to close other audio |
| 6.3 | Leaked internal prompt text appearing in transcript output | CONFIRMED BUG (once) — "Preserve speaker content faithfully" leaked into output | Zero leakage across repeated runs; needs prompt/output separation audit |
| 6.4 | Diarization with a REAL second speaker (not one person doing two voices) | Never actually validated — all tests so far used one person | Speaker A/B labels genuinely track two different voices |
| 6.5 | Summary of a garbled/low-confidence transcript | CONFIRMED ISSUE — summarizer confidently fabricates coherent narrative from noise | Should flag "transcript unclear, summary may be inaccurate" rather than presenting false confidence |
| 6.6 | Summary preserving specific concrete details (amounts, names) vs. over-generalizing | CONFIRMED ISSUE — "3000 rupees, documents missing" got flattened to "personal issues" | Concrete facts preserved, not smoothed away |
| 6.7 | Meeting recording without explicit consent/disclosure UI | CONFIRMED GAP — no consent screen exists yet | Clear disclosure before recording starts, especially once it captures other people's voices |
| 6.8 | Very long meeting (1hr+) — memory/storage/performance | Untested | No degradation, no unbounded memory growth |
| 6.9 | Network drop mid-meeting | Untested | Local buffering, resume/retry, no silent data loss |

